  partName: Ignition Coil Bolt
  description: The Ignition Coil Bolt is a tiny, compact bolt located at the top-center-front
    of the engine, fastening the ignition coil to the engine block. Its primary purpose
    is to provide a secure, stable connection for the ignition coil, enabling reliable
    spark generation and engine operation. Interestingly, the bolt's material, Material.002,
    is designed to resist corrosion and wear, even in harsh engine environments,
    ensuring a durable, long-lasting connection.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
